  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 42a7ef911f4c60e408989a759d2b9b18, type: 3}
  m_Name: SQL_DELETE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.LessonData
  id: SQL_DELETE
  language: 3
  conceptTitle: 'DELETE: Removing Rows'
  symbol: DELETE
  relatedQuestionIds:
  - SQL_07_DELETE
  - SQL_TYPE_09_DELETE
  topics:
  - DELETE
  definition: DELETE removes rows from a table.
  howItWorks: Write DELETE FROM and the table's name, then WHERE and a condition
    that picks the rows to remove. Without WHERE, DELETE removes every row in the
    table, so always check the condition.
  exampleCode: "Table: pets\n id | name  | animal | age\n  1 | Bolt  | Dog    |  
    4\n  2 | Misty | Cat    |   2\n  3 | Rex   | Dog    |   7\n\nDELETE FROM pets\nWHERE
    name = 'Rex';"
  exampleExplanation: Only the row where name is Rex matches the condition, so only
    Rex's row is removed. Bolt and Misty stay in the table.
  tip: DELETE removes whole rows. To change a value inside a row, use UPDATE.
